// The tundra's own animals (V2-10, the first expansion wave), Palearctic and Nearctic: the musk
// ox, the arctic fox, the lemmings whose years of plenty feed everything else, the arctic hare,
// the rock ptarmigan, the snowy owl and the snow bunting. The reindeer, wolverine, ermine, moose
// and willow ptarmigan of the boreal file live here too, as do the gray wolf, red fox and brown
// bear. Values rounded from general mammal and ornithological references and arctic field
// studies; densities for good habitat (lemmings' swing a hundredfold through their cycle).
